## Why This Is Asked

This question probes the ability to combine the Chain of Responsibility with a registry-driven plugin model, enabling runtime composition and reordering of middleware without touching route code.

## Key Concepts

- Chain of Responsibility
- Registry / Plugin architecture
- Dynamic composition and ordering
- Context mutation versus immutability

## Code Example

```typescript
type Context = { [k: string]: any };
type Next = () => Promise<void>;
type Middleware = (ctx: Context, next: Next) => Promise<void>;

class Registry {
  private store = new Map<string, Middleware[]>();
  register(name: string, mw: Middleware) {
    const arr = this.store.get(name) ?? [];
    arr.push(mw); this.store.set(name, arr);
  }
  get(name: string): Middleware[] | undefined {
    return this.store.get(name);
  }
}

function compose(list: Middleware[]): Middleware {
  return async (ctx, next) => {
    let i = -1;
    const dispatch = async (idx: number) => {
      if (idx < 0) return next();
      const mw = list[idx];
      if (!mw) return next();
      await mw(ctx, () => dispatch(idx + 1));
    };
    await dispatch(0);
  };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle middleware cancellation and timeouts without leaking resources?
- How would you test registry composition and ensure order guarantees across deployments?

## Why This Is Asked

This evaluates the ability to design a plugin-friendly, runtime-extensible load balancing system for edge proxies, focusing on decoupling and safe dynamic strategy selection.

## Key Concepts

- Strategy pattern for algorithm abstraction
- Registry-based plugin architecture
- Runtime extensibility without core modifications
- State management for routing decisions
- Isolated testing of individual strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
interface LoadBalancingStrategy {
  selectPeer(route: any, peers: string[], state: any): string;
}

class Registry {
  private map = new Map<string, LoadBalancingStrategy>();

  register(name: string, strategy: LoadBalancingStrategy) {
    this.map.set(name, strategy);
  }

  get(name: string): LoadBalancingStrategy {
    return this.map.get(name);
  }
}

// Example usage
class RoundRobinStrategy implements LoadBalancingStrategy {
  selectPeer(route: any, peers: string[], state: any): string {
    const index = state[route.id] || 0;
    state[route.id] = (index + 1) % peers.length;
    return peers[index];
  }
}

const registry = new Registry();
registry.register('round_robin', new RoundRobinStrategy());
```

